<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How has the European Union’s major recovery plan benefited the 27 member states?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b47314fcf8147aa61b74c335f8185b0d75573b2f53499778a0f85d14186ae417</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:19:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-_600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe--6b8c747aa05e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-%E2%82%AC600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe" /><summary type="html">The 27 member states of the European Union agreed in July 2020 on a €750 billion post-Covid recovery plan called NextGenerationEU. Its main instrument is the Recovery and Resilience Facility, through which the European Commission has already disbursed €450 billion. The programme is due to come to an end in a few months, and countries must claim and account for the remaining funds.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU warns online platforms over livestreaming US execution planned by Pentagon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc16ba010812a171d5c6a4bf3fb8ebd79ca2dd3f718136e148f64c3d13c8ce70</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:05:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon--559bc068ffcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon" /><summary type="html">The European Union warned digital platforms on Monday against livestreaming the execution of Nidal Hasan, a former US Army psychiatrist who is scheduled to be executed by firing squad on December 3 for killing 13 people at a military base in 2009. Under EU rules, platforms have an obligation to moderate shocking and violent content, including capital punishment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO's top US commander warns Russia that any 'foolish' attack on allies would be 'futile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab71a5f04ce7cfe18654aeaae60d2793b0bacc1a34b93c8bfa5a4673e2fd830a</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:41:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile--6a6b5384d4d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile" /><summary type="html">NATO's top US military commander in Europe said Monday that any "foolish" attack on the alliance would be "utterly futile", a warning to Russia as European fears grow over the threat from Moscow that includes "hybrid" warfare and cyberattacks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: NATO's top military commander warns Russia over alleged sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a14e59d256d79abc5a9dd165e690992638933f2b69b677f565465cfe12936264</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:26:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage--36373f6834b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage" /><summary type="html">And as the war in Ukraine continues, Western concerns are growing over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Kiev's wartime backers. NATO's top military commander gave a press conference this Monday from Warsaw. US General Alexus Grynkewich looks set to warn Russia over the alliance’s ability to counter-attack. Analysis by FRANCE 24 International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelensky says learned of Trump's 'energy ceasefire' through media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e0663dfe5c3f6f3e6527da3897df5ae9c36e8a090da593f1f41b55b51b92083</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:24:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media--eb569c8092c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media" /><summary type="html">An Axios report is citing an unnamed US source who says that Donald Trump's surprise energy ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine only concerns oil refineries. Elitsa Gadeva explains what this would mean for both sides.</summary></entry><entry><title>Prison 'Games of Hope' olympics in Italy unite inmates and staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f592bf745f449b48fa68fd722d0bcb5db65f2f9c35f430159d09859d12afc85f</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:54:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/prison-games-of-hope-olympics-in-italy-unite-inmates-and-staff--1ade90bb6eaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/prison-games-of-hope-olympics-in-italy-unite-inmates-and-staff" /><summary type="html">Sport has the power to unite, and overcome barriers... In Rome, inmates and prison officers became athletes for the day, and took part in a sort of mini prison olympics. Organised by the John Paul II foundation for sport, this is the third edition of the “Games of Hope”, over a year after it was held in the men's wing of the prison in 2025. Story by Emily Boyle.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland: Police foils alleged assassination attempt against PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a22fc0e80a2eca304f06b04c76c9271f947d1ac1d3d0d16f210b77216adc4ff4</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:52:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-police-foils-alleged-assassination-attempt-against-pm--e367cf0a729f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-police-foils-alleged-assassination-attempt-against-pm" /><summary type="html">Poland's interior ministry said Sunday a man had been detained on suspicion of plotting an attack against Prime Minister Donald Tusk and Defence minister Wladyslaw Kosiniak-Kamysz. Interior minister Marcin Kierwinski told Polish media that the suspect, a man in his 60s, had been arrested in the southwestern region of Lower Silesia. He was identified through an analysis of content posted online. The man's home is being searched and his contacts examined. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Warsaw, Adrien Sarlat.</summary></entry><entry><title>Are European automakers capable of withstanding Chinese competition?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c8dcad14739eee3e16966df856bea47fd9b8d51634145364ab6d024130dadb9</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:26:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/are-european-automakers-capable-of-withstanding-chinese-competition--242508336086.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/are-european-automakers-capable-of-withstanding-chinese-competition" /><summary type="html">The Paris Motor Show opens its doors today, and with it come mounting economic and diplomatic issues. The European Union has just announced that it has secured a commitment from China to moderate the flow of hybrid vehicles into the block's market. It opens the prospect of cutting China's export by more than a half and could prevent millions of Chinese cars from being shipped to Europe. Are European automakers capable of withstanding this competition and their dependence on China? This report from France 2 and Morgan Ayre.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky says surprised to hear about Trump's 'energy ceasefire' between Ukraine and Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8271944ec66ce51a119b32fa4802fc285c43df444537d87fe4f248d694d2ba41</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:19:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-surprised-to-hear-about-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-between-ukraine-and-russia--2d9571f46443.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-surprised-to-hear-about-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-between-ukraine-and-russia" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian power plants were hit by Russian strikes on Sunday, leading to power outages. President Volodymyr Zelensky announced the attacks and expressed his surprise at the US President's post that stated that an “energy ceasefire” had been agreed upon between Ukraine and Russia. While Zelensky said he was not aware of any deal he said he would welcome one. Moscow has yet to confirm any accord. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>Americans Robert E. Hall and Michael Woodford win Nobel Prize in Economics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:068f971f6286190df0bc24cf82adf3ec8903ed20db5af417550b1c97618242ff</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:54:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-americans-robert-e-hall-and-michael-woodford-win-nobel-prize-in-economics--28f257b26685.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-americans-robert-e-hall-and-michael-woodford-win-nobel-prize-in-economics" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Nobel economics prize has been awarded to US economists ⁠Robert Hall ​and Michael Woodford, the Royal Swedish Academy of ‌Sciences said on Monday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump touts surprise 'energy ceasefire' – Zelensky says he hasn't seen details, Moscow silent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dac357bc2aa1684127e0f71b9809b4375b31c25b217fe01cd9f02d96d33ba30c</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:19:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-trump-touts-surprise-energy-ceasefire-_-zelensky-says-he-hasn-t-seen-details-moscow-silent--30ddc798f98c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-trump-touts-surprise-energy-ceasefire-%E2%80%93-zelensky-says-he-hasn-t-seen-details-moscow-silent" /><summary type="html">The US President Donald Trump sowed confusion on Sunday, announcing an "energy ceasefire" between Ukraine and Russia. Kyiv expressed astonishment, there was silence from Moscow. Ukrainian strikes have wreaked havoc on the Russian oil industry. Were there to be an "energy ceasefire" it could allow Moscow to repair refineries. For Ukraine, it could safeguard vital energy infrastructure. Story by Nicholas Rushworth.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Russia targets Ukraine energy facilities despite Trump ceasefire announcement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:501bb78b3a2f6ea34062dc7bf95548d488a9b642321205e35616aee0c1d41d36</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T05:29:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-live-oil-prices-fall-after-trump-unilaterally-announces-russia-ukraine-energy-ceasefire--87f1573e7c8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-live-oil-prices-fall-after-trump-unilaterally-announces-russia-ukraine-energy-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">Russia continued to attack multiple power plants in Ukraine on Monday, in spite of claims by US President Donald yesterday stating a so-called “energy ceasefire” had been agreed to. NATO chief said that the military alliance would “block, blunt and break” any Russian attack on its members’ territory. Meanwhile strikes on civilians continue, with a 13-year-old girl  among three killed in the country's east. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO top commander to warn Russia over alliance’s ability to counter-attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42db20faf78c41205b67fc2649eef5d45e635d2ab03b9a6f2c6a464d61f981eb</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T01:41:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-top-commander-warn-russia-alliance-counter-attack--fa171fb255f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-top-commander-warn-russia-alliance-counter-attack" /><summary type="html">NATO’s top military commander is expected to warn Russia on Monday that the alliance can counter any attack, officials said. US General Alexus Grynkewich will outline his “theory of victory” at a Warsaw security conference amid Western concerns over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Ukraine’s wartime backers.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Slovenia rejects bill in blow to PM Janez Jansa’s reform agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbc9c0488c99e224a51bc1bc373994b953e2aa471a5715d859c3d1d0f894e4e5</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T22:01:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-slovenia-bill-pm-janez-jansa-reform--8369f436d303.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-slovenia-bill-pm-janez-jansa-reform" /><summary type="html">Slovenians rejected a bill expanding parliamentary inquiry powers in a referendum Sunday, dealing a blow to nationalist Prime Minister Janez Jansa. With 99 percent of votes counted, 51 percent opposed the proposal and 49 percent backed it in the binding vote. The opposition had denounced his reform agenda as "authoritarian".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham warns French voters of Russian political influence on back of Brexit vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a523290bb9e2a477702eb79b0095b20081d4458fcba1e3475dc6830c4c53e46a</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T19:42:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-uk-pm-burnham-warns-french-voters-of-russian-political-influence-on-back-of-brexit-vote--49889e6c39bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-uk-pm-burnham-warns-french-voters-of-russian-political-influence-on-back-of-brexit-vote" /><summary type="html">British Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Sunday warned French and German voters of potential for Russian influence in upcoming elections, on the back of "clear" interference in Britain's referendum on European Union membership in 2016. Russia has previously denied meddling in the Brexit vote, while former British leader Boris Johnson 2020 also said there was no evidence of interference. Burnham made the comments in an interview with The Rest is Politics podcast, released on Sunday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Coerced into a corner?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dceb51e4fe63665f074fae723b8e0240261ac4c16501ef73a2cebcaba3d7dc55</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T17:36:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261011-ukraine-coerced-into-a-corner--d1fdea5bcd74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261011-ukraine-coerced-into-a-corner" /><summary type="html">It's reported that Ukraine is right now facing intense diplomatic pressure and coercion from the Trump administration to end the war quickly.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>New Russian strikes follow Trump's announcement of Russia-Ukraine energy ceasefire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c72be90d017a0c8813dd469cfa64bf786f13838029513516309d67d5897ab5ec</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T14:39:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261011-trump-says-russia-and-ukraine-agree-energy-ceasefire--acf7a15a4061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-trump-says-russia-and-ukraine-agree-energy-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">US President Trump said Sunday via social media platform Truth Social that Russia and Ukraine had agreed to an energy ceasefire. Neither Kyiv nor Moscow confirmed the agreement, but Zelensky later confirmed new Russian strikes to a Ukrainian powerplant. Additional reports suggest at least 5 have been killed and other civilians injured in strikes in the cities of Kharkiv and Ivano-Frankivsk.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: French student protests, October 7 anniversary and Adenot's return to Earth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05e03dc5a86086bc6cfca38651b7536c13964f569ace89341cf749a05d69c049</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T13:17:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-the-week-in-pictures-french-student-protests-october-7-anniversary-and-adenot-return-to-ear--92c20302aefd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-the-week-in-pictures-french-student-protests-october-7-anniversary-and-adenot-return-to-earth" /><summary type="html">Blockades and protests by French secondary school and university students continued, occasionally becoming violent; French astronaut Sophie Adenot returned to Earth after eight months aboard the International Space Station; Israel's commemorations marking the three-year anniversary of the October 7 attacks: here's a look back at some of the most striking images from the past week's news.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo says will undergo surgery for early-stage lung nodule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec4cb8c1ab7b64a1c9c174cf6d08c78571fa397bc14bc82d704783ff032cbad</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T10:34:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-pope-leo-says-will-undergo-surgery-for-early-stage-lung-nodule--110af765b1d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-pope-leo-says-will-undergo-surgery-for-early-stage-lung-nodule" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV said Sunday he would undergo surgery in the coming days for a lung nodule detected at an early stage.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says ready to halt refinery strikes if Moscow stops energy attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc47504440a7a052b6152c05d447123664256317cd26f088c1f821db18cf32a6</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T10:21:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-ukraine-ready-halt-refinery-strikes-if-moscow-stops-energy-attacks-zelensky-says--6653602e82d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-ukraine-ready-halt-refinery-strikes-if-moscow-stops-energy-attacks-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Sunday said Kyiv was ready to halt strikes Russian oil refineries if Moscow stopped attacks on Ukrainian energy infrastructure. Zelensky also pushed back on US President Donald Trump's comments made Saturday evening calling for Ukraine to elect a new leader by saying, "It's up to our people".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish PM Sanchez kicks off election campaign amid housing crisis protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca69604a914b4ae59d33aecf78e93c362e5271e01bbec29afe9f0886fb80211c</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T07:46:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-spanish-pm-sanchez-kicks-off-election-campaign-amid-housing-crisis-protests--31069b0fb951.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261011-spanish-pm-sanchez-kicks-off-election-campaign-amid-housing-crisis-protests" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez launched his campaign for a snap November election on Saturday. The vote comes as a deepening housing crisis is driving protests and putting pressure on his left-wing coalition.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Zelensky clash over diesel deal as Russian strikes on Ukraine kill at least 21</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a954a921c6fafdaa8393839816ddff03c8e366572bd7c58b6366779d770e1c6</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:39:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-trump-zelensky-clash-over-diesel-deal-as-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-kill-21-including-child--ee33fd4d2e87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-trump-zelensky-clash-over-diesel-deal-as-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-kill-21-including-children" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday told reporters that Ukraine should "get a new president", adding that his Ukrainian counterpart Volodymyr Zelensky had disobeyed his orders not to strike Russian refineries. This came after Washington moved to ease sanctions on Russian diesel and as Moscow's strikes on Ukraine, including the city of Zaporizhzhia, killed at least 21 people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says Ukraine needs new president after Zelensky pushes back on diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a36f7e5a978d0b0579465c6303635b240586524fe8628c3efd82a25fc68a5872</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T08:41:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-live-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-zaporizhzhia-kill-least-seven-including-children--2e66a7264c75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-live-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-zaporizhzhia-kill-least-seven-including-children" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday said that Ukraine needs a new president “who can make a deal” to end the war, and called on Ukrainian ‌President Volodymyr ⁠Zelensky to his forces from targeting Russian oil refineries. This came after Washington moved to ease sanctions on Russian diesel and Moscow's continued strikes on Ukraine killed at least 21 people, including four children. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'All human emotions': French astronaut Sophie Adenot returns to Earth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6214af4540776bc5eb66b3c85e4ea62e79e0cbeaac4d5e7579acb8acb94e3958</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T08:09:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-all-human-emotion-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-first-words-since-returning-earth--55457d343553.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-all-human-emotion-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-first-words-since-returning-earth" /><summary type="html">French astronaut Sophie Adenot said she experienced “the full range of human emotions, from the most joyful to the most difficult” during her eight months in space, speaking on Saturday in Cologne, Germany, in her first public appearance since returning to Earth.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>‘So safe you could drink it’: Scientists and pesticide victims fear an EU rollback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a970ae95552bb6347cc80106baa149ce4a8532953a80650891839829e25a1c09</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T07:10:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-so-safe-you-could-drink-it-scientists-and-pesticide-victims-fear-an-eu-rollback--79f5867b4455.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-so-safe-you-could-drink-it-scientists-and-pesticide-victims-fear-an-eu-rollback" /><summary type="html">For decades, French farmers sprayed pesticides they were told were harmless. Many have since fallen ill, grappling with cancers and other diseases caused by exposure. As the EU prepares to vote on a package that would end regular safety reviews of most pesticides, victims, doctors and scientists warn it could keep harmful products on the market for longer.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italy's biggest-ever wine heist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5220bf852904efa03ca1841bda048440833d56bfec70d2a2b6db3bf1b51e2e6b</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T20:08:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-italy-s-biggest-ever-wine-heist--5d4a20ca2b50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-italy-s-biggest-ever-wine-heist" /><summary type="html">A multi million euro wine heist in Italy. As thieves in Tuscany steal 30 thousand bottles of the one of the most iconic labels in the country from a warehouse of the the prized Marchesi Antinori winery as it prepared for a major export. The company said in the past few hours, they believe two vans and up to six thieves were involved. Gavin Lee speaks to France 24's correspondent in Rome, Seema Gupta.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump strikes diesel deal with Putin, reversing years of pressure on Russia over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa2df65073088a11b5aa94424f5b4ff3265d3f9239935b326781631ab8c68aa0</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T20:00:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-trump-strikes-diesel-deal-with-putin-reversing-years-of-pressure-on-russia-over-ukraine-war--81c65c075c6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-trump-strikes-diesel-deal-with-putin-reversing-years-of-pressure-on-russia-over-ukraine-war" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that Russia had agreed to immediately supply more than 300,000 tonnes of diesel to US and global markets in an effort to cut fuel prices before November's midterm elections. The move marks a stunning change of policy after the US and its allies hit Russia with waves of sanctions over its invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU's Covid recovery fund was 'absolutely a success': European Court of Auditors' Pierre Moscovici</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d0f464b6e117ae65e32b9ee04b5dccac058a6a303b3555f4be00914799df6df</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:51:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-eu-s-covid-recovery-fund-was-absolutely-a-success-european-court-of-auditors-pierre-moscovi--05c75909711a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261009-eu-s-covid-recovery-fund-was-absolutely-a-success-european-court-of-auditors-pierre-moscovici" /><summary type="html">2020 was an annus horribilis. Covid stalked the land. Lockdowns, curfews and social distancing were the order of the day. But there was a silver lining: European countries showed themselves to be capable of great solidarity, jointly procuring vaccines and then agreeing on a mammoth post-Covid recovery fund, the Recovery and Resilience Facility (RRF). That fund has disbursed €450 billion in grants and loans to EU member states since 2021. As the RRF enters its crucial final phase, we take stock of the situation with Pierre Moscovici, the French member of the European Court of Auditors (ECA).</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Israel a rare dissenting voice as praise pours in for Nobel Peace Prize winner Navi Pillay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c270715b7df3a7aa263465e9ceed4c742e0c6d3e283a652aeb0dd0a8f98a50c3</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:20:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-israel-a-rare-dissenting-voice-as-praise-pours-in-for-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay--0ac82efe71b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-israel-a-rare-dissenting-voice-as-praise-pours-in-for-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay" /><summary type="html">Advocates of human rights and international justice cheered, even as Israeli officials fumed, after South African jurist and former UN human rights chief Navi Pillay won the Nobel Peace Prize on Friday. The 85-year-old drew wide praise for decades of work, including investigating crimes in Rwanda, Israel and the occupied Palestinian territories.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>International Criminal Court faces 'test of resilience' as US imposes sweeping sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef8d3937c91f706388511ccd2a945a61dee7ced6101bad0bee445c281f6bfd2e</id><updated>2026-10-12T18:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:19:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-international-criminal-court-faces-test-of-resilience-as-us-imposes-sweeping-sanctions--8a8a0bb4e4e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261009-international-criminal-court-faces-test-of-resilience-as-us-imposes-sweeping-sanctions" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has imposed sweeping new sanctions on the International Criminal Court as part of its campaign to dismantle what it describes as a "rogue" tribunal, threatening to cripple its operations. Following the move, ⁠the European Union said it was "ready to take any necessary measures to enable the court to carry out its work".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
